# Card visual system (ModularCards RPG)

## Rarity (Uncommon cancelled)

Do **not** use Uncommon going forward. Plan to remove `CardRarity.UNCOMMON` from pools/UI when touching card systems.

| Rarity | Pack color (banner + corner) |
|--------|------------------------------|
| Basic | brown |
| Common | green |
| Rare | blue |
| Epic | purple |
| Legendary | yellow (gold) |
| Curse | gray frame + red accents (banner/corner/socket) |

## Class → main card color

Class owns `border` + `container` (+ optional BG tint).

| Class / family | Pack color |
|----------------|------------|
| Warrior / tank line (Paladin for now) | blue |
| Trapper (later) | TBD (not blue — avoid clash with Rare) |
| Curse | gray + red |

If class color equals a rarity color (e.g. Warrior blue vs Rare blue), rarity must stay readable via **banner + corner pair**, not border alone.

## Layer map (Zsprites ModularCards)

```
BG / border / container  →  Class
banner + corner          →  Rarity
energy_*                 →  Energy cost slot only
socket_* (color)         →  Card type (Attack / Defense / Utility / Power…)
gem (optional)           →  extra accent, not required for Early Alpha
```

## Upgrade (STS-style)

- Do **not** bake a separate upgraded frame.
- Name: `CardName+`
- Name text turns green (cost number green if cost decreased).
- Same class/rarity layers as base card.

## Layout (ModularCards — confirmed mockup)

Top → bottom on card face (banner is **between** art and description, not STS2 top title):

1. Energy orb top-left (`energy_*` matching class color + cost label)
2. **Art** — smaller upper panel (`container` / art slot)
3. **Name** — middle `banner` (white/light text; upgraded = name+ green)
4. **Description** — larger lower panel (`description_*`)
5. Type signal — short type text in description area and/or colored `socket` (not required on every frame bake)

Reference stack (Warrior Basic example from mockup):
- Class blue: `border_blue` + blue energy orb
- Rarity brown: `banner_brown` + `corner_brown`
- Light art/desc panels: `BG_white` / `description_white` (+ optional innercorners)

